{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nThe project Jira target is Jira Cloud (`https://navasage.atlassian.net`), while `reconciler.rich_text_cutover` defaults to `off`. Enable the already-shipped and tested Markdown↔ADF bridge behavior for this project without enabling the unrelated Data Center wire. This ticket is configuration enablement only; codec correctness remains covered by the existing rich-text unit and live-integration suites.\n\n## Plan\n- Add a `[reconciler]` table to the project `rebar.toml`.\n- Set `rich_text_cutover = \"cloud\"`.\n- Run `rebar config` from the worktree. This loads the typed config, rejects invalid enum values, and reports each resolved value with its precedence source.\n- Check the exact `reconciler.rich_text_cutover` output line and run `git diff --check`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `rebar.toml` contains `[reconciler]` with `rich_text_cutover = \"cloud\"`; verify by inspecting the focused git diff.\n- [ ] `rebar config` exits successfully, proving the typed loader accepts the value.\n- [ ] `rebar config` reports `reconciler.rich_text_cutover = cloud [project]`, proving both the resolved value and project-config provenance.\n- [ ] `git diff --check` reports no whitespace errors."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787005171020040001,"uuid":"444fbd8f-cef2-4864-a5c1-5b7d4ff0e4cb"}